rce":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"eccd8f4aa78ca8f84431634a3fb82acbd773ba0478854ed81ec9873ddfd86a51","quote":"The Ermenegildo Zegna Group operates in the personal luxury goods market, which includes the following product segments: accessories, jewelry, beauty, apparel and watches. By product, we primarily focus on the apparel and accessories segments of the personal luxury goods market. The luxury textiles market, which accounts for 7% of the Group’s consolidated revenues after eliminations, is not discussed in this section.","context":"Industry information contained in this section is based on the Bain-Altagamma Luxury Goods Worldwide Market Study, Fall 2025 (the “Bain-Altagamma Study”), unless otherwise indicated.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":442,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"a9e5042cc03f69e879a92be8bfb251cec306f05fdcef47300724eafdf36e4a85","quote":"Demand in the personal luxury goods market, especially in the absolute luxury segment, is characterized by a low price-sensitivity. Instead, demand is more likely driven by tangible and intangible factors which fuel brand equity and desirability. Brand equity is made of several important components, including heritage, exclusivity, recognizability, quality, and experience.","context":"The Ermenegildo Zegna Group operates in the personal luxury goods market, which includes the following product segments: accessories, jewelry, beauty, apparel and watches. By product, we primarily focus on the apparel and accessories segments of the personal luxury goods market. The luxury textiles market, which accounts for 7% of the Group’s consolidated revenues after eliminations, is not discussed in this section.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":443,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"d554d3f65bc42eb497a643766e969cef6e2d5b788fdfdf626a2e3857ee51dd0e","quote":"According to the Bain-Altagamma Study, in 2025 the global personal luxury goods market had a total estimated value of approximately €358 billion. After a steady growth for more than two decades with a compound annual growth rate (“CAGR”) of approximately 6% from 1996 to 2019 and approximately 5% from 2019 to 2024, the personal luxury goods market experienced a mild decrease in 2024 (approximately -2% as compared to 2023) and is expected to decrease by approximately 2% in 2025 as compared to 2024, in each case at current exchange rates.","context":"Demand in the personal luxury goods market, especially in the absolute luxury segment, is characterized by a low price-sensitivity. Instead, demand is more likely driven by tangible and intangible factors which fuel brand equity and desirability. Brand equity is made of several important components, including heritage, exclusivity, recognizability, quality, and experience.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":444,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"fd127c16153f04d1e9cdb338e81dc21493110b8c1be67a8561ec498a9d543b4d","quote":"The chart below sets forth the evolution of sales in the global personal luxury goods market from 1996 to 2025 (the data for 2025 being an estimate).","context":"32","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":446,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"e8cbefb093c2caf899e9e9128f9d0998551473038d4a797b54e0d47d11995f20","quote":"Source: Bain-Altagamma Luxury Goods Worldwide Market Study, Fall 2025, dated November 20, 2025.","context":"Personal Luxury Goods Market Evolution – €bn","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":448,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"d317b7da22fb23266dc8193ce7d98bd544aa870ce1651dea4433c06465ec51d0","quote":"The Bain-Altagamma Study estimates the personal luxury goods market to reach the range between €365-375bn in 2026 with a growth of 3-5% at constant exchange rates as compared to 2025, with the United States leading the growth, supported by robust financial markets, Europe and Japan demonstrating continued resilience and China progressing with a steady recovery.","context":"Source: Bain-Altagamma Luxury Goods Worldwide Market Study, Fall 2025, dated November 20, 2025.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":449,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"3365267796f385de8619e12f8224c81fe57ad057ba0f73fe7b6212e5a9a3002d","quote":"The personal luxury goods market is characterized by significant barriers to entry, such as, among others: (i) brand heritage, which is embodied by unreplaceable assets like a brand’s history, values and DNA; (ii) brand equity, which is the perception of the uniqueness and high reputation of a brand, built over time with, among the others, important investments in advertising; (iii) know-how, characterized by many aspects of the “saper fare” (savoir faire) starting from the design and innovation capacity through the ability to provide products with a superior quality and an utmost experience for clients, and (iv) a high-end distribution network, which embraces prime locations in the most important, highly competitive, luxury streets and malls.","context":"The Bain-Altagamma Study estimates the personal luxury goods market to reach the range between €365-375bn in 2026 with a growth of 3-5% at constant exchange rates as compared to 2025, with the United States leading the growth, supported by robust financial markets, Europe and Japan demonstrating continued resilience and China progressing with a steady recovery.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":450,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"f8a323f05dfdbdf51112a3a050f49ac7e170a3e906131df43e18bff5c13af229","quote":"Group Competitive Strengths and Strategic Vision","context":"The personal luxury goods market is characterized by significant barriers to entry, such as, among others: (i) brand heritage, which is embodied by unreplaceable assets like a brand’s history, values and DNA; (ii) brand equity, which is the perception of the uniqueness and high reputation of a brand, built over time with, among the others, important investments in advertising; (iii) know-how, characterized by many aspects of the “saper fare” (savoir faire) starting from the design and innovation capacity through the ability to provide products with a superior quality and an utmost experience for clients, and (iv) a high-end distribution network, which embraces prime locations in the most important, highly competitive, luxury streets and malls.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":451,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"8fa408f3ff238682bcd780b57bfdadccd9d8599f0117bd8d6f2dc5f92808b15a","quote":"As Ermenegildo Zegna Group, we operate in the personal luxury goods market. Although in this arena we compete with other global companies, we believe we have unique advantages to successfully further strengthen our presence and leading position. Heritage, Italian craftsmanship, undisputed legacy along with a portfolio of complementary brands with significant untapped growth potentials represent strong and prime assets for the Group.","context":"Competitive Strengths","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":453,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"6dea7bda4a526b107951b4dc3bded1cb3f9182172d89fef0c0bcf2153df1423a","quote":"We believe that the following key competitive strengths have been the primary drivers of the Group’s historic success and continue to be pillars of its future growth strategy.","context":"As Ermenegildo Zegna Group, we operate in the personal luxury goods market. Although in this arena we compete with other global companies, we believe we have unique advantages to successfully further strengthen our presence and leading position. Heritage, Italian craftsmanship, undisputed legacy along with a portfolio of complementary brands with significant untapped growth potentials represent strong and prime assets for the Group.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":454,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"2922612a51f3929140b9a77b38910b1dd893ad03712d90a3ea24deeecd983461","quote":"Since the foundation of Lanificio Ermenegildo Zegna e Figli S.p.A. (“Lanificio” or “Lanificio Ermenegildo Zegna”) at the beginning of the past century, the name Zegna has been synonymous with quality, style and innovation for men’s fashion. This has been and continues to be true for the ZEGNA brand and the Ermenegildo Zegna Group.","context":"Heritage","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":456,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"f0ab368c809f24c0f38b7a9735ee273df58741826b086dff5b6740485cb03e1e","quote":"The Ermenegildo Zegna Group has a consolidated leadership position in luxury menswear, rooted on its 116-years of history. This undisputed legacy, along with a portfolio of unique and complementary brands, constitutes the Group’s main competitive strength. ZEGNA has evolved from being one of the most recognized brands in men’s tailoring to become an","context":"Luxury Menswear Leadership","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":458,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"dd01b3d13f7e40d09ba3f06042daa6f5f80d3a3293c1704913045ce796fb4f9f","quote":"iconic brand in the men’s timeless luxury segment with a top-class retail network in the most important luxury streets and shopping malls. The addition of Thom Browne in 2018 and TOM FORD FASHION in 2023 has further strengthened the Group’s leadership by capturing distinctive and complementary segments of clientele, including also women, while leveraging on the Group’s textile and manufacturing know-how.","context":"33","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":460,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"d9c29ab4b3e5971c45355e92ff1fcfc63945880c266067b01cc5e969b5af2da5","quote":"The Ermenegildo Zegna Group controls an integrated luxury textiles and manufacturing chain, vertically integrated from the sourcing of the finest raw material to the production of high-quality garments. Through the historical Lanificio Ermenegildo Zegna as well as the more recent acquisitions of Dondi, Bonotto, Tessitura Ubertino, and the minority interests in Filati Biagioli Modesto, the Group has built an in-house textiles platform that provides a unique competitive hedge in term of innovation capacity and research of the finest and highest performing fabrics with the best quality.","context":"Luxury Filiera","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":462,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"ba63581d54acd77f279db6799b068e6509fcf404f18c7d13084d0a2bda6f002f","quote":"The textile platform, integrated with state-of-the-art manufacturing capabilities, represents a key competitive advantage that the Group can offer to the brands in its portfolio. It also constitutes a significant barrier to entry in the strategic Su Misura (Made-to-Measure) business. The Group offers personalized Su Misura products for its three brands with best-in-class lead time ranging from 2 weeks in certain key stores (particularly for ZEGNA) to 4 or 6 weeks. Management believes that the breadth of the offering and the lead times, as well as the service quality and the experience provided to customers, are setting standards in the industry. These services enable us to cultivate meaningful client relationships, develop a loyal customer base and drive new customer engagement.","context":"The Ermenegildo Zegna Group controls an integrated luxury textiles and manufacturing chain, vertically integrated from the sourcing of the finest raw material to the production of high-quality garments. Through the historical Lanificio Ermenegildo Zegna as well as the more recent acquisitions of Dondi, Bonotto, Tessitura Ubertino, and the minority interests in Filati Biagioli Modesto, the Group has built an in-house textiles platform that provides a unique competitive hedge in term of innovation capacity and research of the finest and highest performing fabrics with the best quality.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":463,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"7ff23228c9d42f6ff66f57748b5b889fb9796db4e490b41cd52f21daf8834be1","quote":"Complementary Portfolio of Uniquely Positioned Luxury Brands","context":"The textile platform, integrated with state-of-the-art manufacturing capabilities, represents a key competitive advantage that the Group can offer to the brands in its portfolio. It also constitutes a significant barrier to entry in the strategic Su Misura (Made-to-Measure) business. The Group offers personalized Su Misura products for its three brands with best-in-class lead time ranging from 2 weeks in certain key stores (particularly for ZEGNA) to 4 or 6 weeks. Management believes that the breadth of the offering and the lead times, as well as the service quality and the experience provided to customers, are setting standards in the industry. These services enable us to cultivate meaningful client relationships, develop a loyal customer base and drive new customer engagement.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":464,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"e89fc465562e3a4f9c4b0b98a9e4107ca0cdbcec68f004925b13996d44b6c55f","quote":"Ermenegildo Zegna Group is made of three brands complementary across styles, occasions of use, and aesthetic.","context":"Complementary Portfolio of Uniquely Positioned Luxury Brands","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":465,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"4d1d59ab6db8b541c22ecbdff589252f9ac0097d7e1143e02c4c4a75e89af7d2","quote":"ZEGNA. The Group’s eponymous brand is a leading brand in the men’s timeless luxury segment. Authenticity represents the brand’s core and true value. The brand’s authenticity is grounded not only on 116 years of unique heritage but also in a responsible vision that began at its foundation and has been passed down through the generations, ensuring that giving back, responsibility towards the environment and community well-being remain key values for the brand. An expression of this vision is a freely accessible natural area covering approximately 100 square kilometers from the small village of Trivero, where the Group originated, to the peaks of the Biella Alps in Italy. This area was created by the Group’s founder around 100 years ago and rebranded “Oasi Zegna” in 1993. Oasi Zegna has been and continues to be an important source of inspiration for the ZEGNA brand’s collections and for the brand iconic products.","context":"Ermenegildo Zegna Group is made of three brands complementary across styles, occasions of use, and aesthetic.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":466,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"cb7ff16d7bd6e23468596eb636585b39fddb3e2dfeba7c2af1ab42bc78b64e03","quote":"Thom Browne. Distinctive craftsmanship, undisputed tailoring know-how and proud community are the key ingredients of the brand success in both men and womenswear. Thom Browne has a wide range of luxury and fashion clients that appreciate the unique design and quality.","context":"ZEGNA. The Group’s eponymous brand is a leading brand in the men’s timeless luxury segment. Authenticity represents the brand’s core and true value. The brand’s authenticity is grounded not only on 116 years of unique heritage but also in a responsible vision that began at its foundation and has been passed down through the generations, ensuring that giving back, responsibility towards the environment and community well-being remain key values for the brand. An expression of this vision is a freely accessible natural area covering approximately 100 square kilometers from the small village of Trivero, where the Group originated, to the peaks of the Biella Alps in Italy. This area was created by the Group’s founder around 100 years ago and rebranded “Oasi Zegna” in 1993. Oasi Zegna has been and continues to be an important source of inspiration for the ZEGNA brand’s collections and for the brand iconic products.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":467,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000015/zgn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de.bin","sha256":"f8f4038cdd1a137744997a6b8c22af5a01f42c9009924b340e3cf5f63eb8e8de"}},{"id":"fe2ac272f874059fd3b34c1b64272554d1da28364c43134cb47b36ad88eefce8","quote":"TOM FORD FASHION. Added to the Group in 2023, TOM FORD FASHION completes the Group’s offering delivering an alluringly modern aesthetic for a client who pursues recognition, product excellence and impeccable fit.","context":"Thom Browne. Distinctive craftsmanship, undisputed tailoring know-how and proud community are the key ingredients of the brand success in both men and womenswear. Thom Browne has a wide range of luxury and fashion clients that appreciate the unique design and quality.","section":"ITEM 4 INFORMATION ON THE COMPANY","block":468,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000015","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-03-20","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.se